%S A398639 0,0,1,4,27,208,1958,21879,284331,4190340,68693115
%N A398639 Number of connected quasi-cubic graphs on 2*n + 1 vertices.
%C A398639 A quasi-cubic graph is a simple graph with one vertex of degree 4 and all other vertices of degree 3. By the handshake lemma, such a graph necessarily has odd order.
%H A398639 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/ConnectedGraph.html">Connected Graph</a>.
%H A398639 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Quasi-CubicGraph.html">Quasi-Cubic Graph</a>.
%e A398639 a(4) = 27 because 27 of the 28 quasi-cubic graphs on 9 vertices are connected.
%Y A398639 Cf. A398638 (not-necessarily-connected quasi-cubic graphs).
%Y A398639 Cf. A398640 (quasi-quintic graphs).
%Y A398639 Cf. A398641 (connected quasi-quintic graphs).
